module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.construct_field_value_not_typed_against_the_record_declaration

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data construct_field_value_not_typed_against_the_record_declaration: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "construct_field_value_not_typed_against_the_record_declaration" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a record construct whose field value does not inhabit that field's declared type is ACCEPTED by v2.compiler.infer. `type ArB { n: Int, m: Int }` with `data ar_bad: ArB = ArB { n: true, m: 3 }`: `n` holds a Bool where the record declares an Int.",
    "SPECIMEN AS FOUND, measured by execution (2026-09-30, sleek-fox-423, gunbc#12740 head): a headed construct resolved through v2.compiler.name_resolve resolve_with_admission_context_policy and handed to v2.compiler.infer infer. Resolve accepts and the construct's tag is the record's declaration reference; infer answered Accepted. The headless spelling gets the same verdict after resolve elaborates its tag, so the gap was in infer's construct typing and not in how the tag was written. The specimen was first filed with Bool-declared fields holding `m: 3`; that spelling is one of the two populations still counted below, so the row's specimen is the Int-declared form, which is the one that refuses.",
    "WHY INFER DID NOT SEE IT: its declared-type judgments had two producers, a call argument at its formal and an Arrow body at its declared return. No site took a construct's resolved record declaration and judged each field value against the field the record declares, and a construct's own type was the product of its children, which never derived because its tag is a reference.",
    "HARM: below the ordinary compiler floor. DESIGN section 4b names 'values inhabit declared types' among the floor properties whose failure is a below-baseline regression. It was silent: no diagnostic, and a downstream emitter or evaluator received a construct its declaration says cannot exist.",
    "THE REPAIR (the change that rewrote this row): a record construct is its constructor applied by name. v2.compiler.infer infer_record_construct_facts reads the fields the record declares, pairs each with the value that fills it through the one binding plan (v2.std.arrow_signature application_binding_plan_over), and judges each pair through the one judge (infer_judge_declared_position) at a third position, v2.std.inhabitance PositionRecordField, under one instantiation of the record's binders (infer_judge_formal_args, the application's own walk). A missing, undeclared or twice-named field refuses; each refusal names the record, the field and, for a value, the declared and produced types. The construct's type is the declared record, instantiated at its binders.",
    "CURRENT RUNG, PER PATH, on the v2 resolve-to-infer route. STRUCTURALLY GUARANTEED (3): the field SET of every record construct, in any module; and the field VALUES of a record declared in the subject module whose field type is Int or Bool, one of the record's own type variables, or a declaration the subject module resolves (a nested record). BELOW THAT, COUNTED AND NOT SILENT, two populations, each an Accepted construct carrying an UndecidableFormalUnresolved obligation at the value and staying on the frontier: (a) a record declared in ANOTHER module, because v2.compiler.resolve ResolvedTree resolved_declarations holds only the subject module's declarations with resolved bodies and symbol_index holds a declaration as authored; (b) a field declared as a kernel type that has no value-type node in a v2 std authority, and so no row in v2.extdeps.languages.dag dag_kernel_value_type_roster: Float, Secret, Json, Unit and Bytes, each rostered as kernel_type_<name>_has_no_v2_value_type_node. Int and Bool are judged: the roster made the resolver's binding and the denotation join's key one symbol, which for Bool they had not been. The class's rung is the minimum across these paths, so the class as a whole is NOT at 3 and this row stays open.",
    "CEILING: structurally guaranteed. A declaration can always be spelled with a value of the wrong type, so the state is writable in source; what is attainable is that no Accepted program contains one. Both remaining populations are decidable and fully modelled, so neither is a ceiling.",
    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGERS, at capability grain. (a) CROSS-MODULE: v2 infer reads the RESOLVED member types of any declaration a reference resolves to, across modules. That is gunbc#12726 PR2 (royal-stag-371, branch session/royal-stag-371-pr2-declaration-bodies): declaration-body types resolved once per ingest in the declaring module's scope, with every reader of resolved_declarations cut over in the same motion. It is sufficient for this row only when the record construct reader in v2.compiler.infer (infer_record_formals) reads that provider, so that a construct of a record declared in another module is judged field by field; the capability is shared with callee signatures, field projection and match fields (gunbc#12506). (b) KERNEL TYPES WITHOUT A VALUE-TYPE NODE: each of the five rows above names its own trigger, the std authority owning a value-type node for that type and the roster carrying a row for it. Neither trigger is satisfied by a hand-built tree carrying the binding.",
    "ENROLLED EVIDENCE, all on the real route from source text: v2.test.claim.compiler.infer_record_construct_field_inhabitance_witness_test. The discriminating red is rcf_a_field_value_of_the_wrong_type_refuses_holds with rcf_the_refusal_names_the_record_the_field_and_both_types_holds; the positive control, one term away and asserted DECIDED, is rcf_inhabiting_field_values_are_accepted_and_decided_holds, with a generic and a nested control beside it. The cross-module population is pinned as it is by rcf_a_cross_module_records_field_value_is_counted_not_judged_holds, which goes red when its trigger lands and is then rewritten to assert the refusal. The Bool-declared field was pinned the same way until the kernel value-type roster landed, and is now the refusal rcf_a_bool_declared_field_value_of_the_wrong_type_refuses_holds.",
    "RELATED, NOT THE SAME CLASS: zero_field_construction_escapes_the_field_set_check (a missing field, measured on the v1 path) and optional_admitted_where_a_required_value_is_declared (optionality at a Required position). VARIANT constructs are not this row's subject either: a construct whose tag is a coproduct's variant keeps product introduction and stays on the counted frontier."
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.infer", decl_name: "infer_record_construct_facts", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.infer", decl_name: "infer_record_formals", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.std.inhabitance", decl_name: "position_record_field", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.compiler.infer_record_construct_field_inhabitance_witness_test", decl_name: "rcf_a_field_value_of_the_wrong_type_refuses_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.compiler.infer_record_construct_field_inhabitance_witness_test", decl_name: "rcf_inhabiting_field_values_are_accepted_and_decided_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.compiler.infer_record_construct_field_inhabitance_witness_test", decl_name: "rcf_a_cross_module_records_field_value_is_counted_not_judged_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.compiler.infer_record_construct_field_inhabitance_witness_test", decl_name: "rcf_a_bool_declared_field_value_of_the_wrong_type_refuses_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
